      "locator": {"page": 175, "equation": "8.45", "figure": null, "panel": null, "section": "8.8"},
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "curator_note": "Path labeled 'i' (inductive / charge-site cleavage) of Eq 8.45. Book draws 0 electron-pushing arcs: the scheme shows only three labeled reaction arrows (i, alpha, sigma) from the molecular ion to competing products, no fishhooks. The single move <1> -- heterolytic cleavage of the C2-O3 bond with both bonding electrons going to oxygen -- is an implicit move required for electron balance (not drawn on the page). Precursor is the n-ionized molecular ion of neopentyl alcohol (2,2-dimethyl-1-propanol) with charge and odd electron localized on O per the book's (CH3)3C-CH2-O(+.)H drawing; the C-O bonding pair migrates to O, leaving the (CH3)3CCH2+ cation and the .OH radical (oxygen keeps its pre-existing odd electron, so its non-bonding population rises by 2 into a lone pair while the radical count is unchanged -- the soft lone-pair note is expected). m/z 71.0855 is the curator-computed monoisotopic value of (CH3)3CCH2+; the page prints the 1% abundance but no m/z."
    },
